/// What happened to the patient's Keycloak identity when the invite was sent.
///
/// Separate from PatientPortalInviteStatus because they answer different questions. The
/// invite status says whether the invitation is still live; this says whether the patient
/// can act on it at all. An invite can be perfectly valid while the account behind it was
/// never created, which is exactly the failure staff need to see rather than discover from
/// a patient who cannot sign in.
enum PortalInviteIdentityStatus {
  /// Phone-only invite, or an invite issued before this was recorded.
  NOT_REQUESTED
  /// We created the identity and sent it password and verification actions.
  PROVISIONED
  /// The identity already existed and still has setup to finish.
  EXISTING_PENDING
  /// The patient already has a working account; nothing was sent.
  ALREADY_ACTIVE
  /// No service-account credentials are configured on this deployment.
  SKIPPED
  /// Keycloak refused or could not be reached. identityFailureReason says which.
  FAILED
}

/// Where a staff invitation is in its life. Mirrors PatientPortalInviteStatus, with ACCEPTED
/// in place of CLAIMED because nothing is being claimed: a role is being granted.
